      "background": "Payments was deployed from release 1.3 to 1.5, and the gateway balance_cache_ttl_s was changed by an operator from 0.5 to 600 s. Primary fraud screening began timing out, and a reconciliation session held a write lock on the ledger.",
      "assessment": "Primary screening timed out (p95 1023 ms against 15 ms), so the incident commander failed screening over to its standby, and that worked. The commander also ended the reconciliation session holding the ledger lock, which cleared it, and rolled payments back from 1.5 to 1.3 to stop duplicate payments. It then restored gateway balance_cache_ttl_s from 600 to 0.5 so balances are no longer stale.",
      "recommendation": "The operations team has been asked (soon priority) to find and correct the ledger records behind 'duplicate payments = 38', and to review any money effect on customers; the incident commander cannot change data. Find out why primary screening slowed before failing back, and fix payments 1.5 before redeploying it."
